Time Complexity:

Let n = size of array

    Single traversal using three pointers → O(n)

Overall: O(n)


Space Complexity:

    In-place sorting (only pointers used)

Overall: O(1)


Approach:

1. Initialize three pointers:
   - low = 0
   - mid = 0
   - high = n - 1

2. Traverse while mid <= high:

   - If nums[mid] == 0:
     → Swap nums[low] and nums[mid]
     → Increment low and mid

   - If nums[mid] == 2:
     → Swap nums[mid] and nums[high]
     → Decrement high
     → Do not increment mid
       (new element at mid needs checking)

   - If nums[mid] == 1:
     → Increment mid

3. Continue until all elements are sorted

4. Array gets partitioned into:
   - 0’s region
   - 1’s region
   - 2’s region




class Solution {
    public void sortColors(int[] nums) {
        //Dutch National Flag Algo
        int low = 0;
        int mid = 0;
        int high = nums.length-1;
        while(mid<=high){
            if(nums[mid]==0){
                int temp = nums[low];
                nums[low] = nums[mid];
                nums[mid] = temp;
                low++;
                mid++;
            }
            else if(nums[mid]==2){
                int temp = nums[high];
                nums[high] = nums[mid];
                nums[mid] = temp;
                high--;
            }
            else{
                mid++;
            }
        }
    }
}



